.TH CF-CI-CD 1 "September 2026" "cf-cli v1.1.2" "Cloudflare CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
cf-ci-cd.1 \- CI/CD and pipeline automation recipes with cf
.PP
Integrating \fBcf\fR into automated deployment pipelines (such as GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or CircleCI) allows you to automate edge deployments, cache purging, DNS validation, and database operations.
.PP
.PP
.SH 1. AUTOMATION PRINCIPLES
.PP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAlways pass \fB--yes\fR\fR: Destructive operations (such as \fBdelete\fR or \fBpurge\fR) require interactive confirmation by default. In headless environments, pass \fB--yes\fR to auto-confirm without blocking on stdin.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAuthenticate via Repository Secrets\fR: Supply \fBCF\fIAPI\fRTOKEN\fR (or \fBCLOUDFLARE\fIAPI\fRTOKEN\fR) via secure environment variables. Never hardcode credentials.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUse JSON Output for Pipeline Parsing\fR: Pass \fB--output json\fR and pipe directly into \fBjq\fR to extract values for subsequent workflow steps.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBExit Codes\fR:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB0\fR: Success
.IP \(bu 2
\fB1\fR: API error, invalid arguments, or authentication failure
.PP
.PP
.SH 2. GITHUB ACTIONS WORKFLOW EXAMPLES
.PP
.SS "Example A: Automatic Cache Purge on Website Deploy"
Purge edge cache whenever new assets are deployed to your origin:
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
name: Deploy & Purge Cache

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Install Bun
        uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@v2

      - name: Install cf CLI
        run: bun install -g @agileguy/cf-cli

      - name: Purge Cloudflare Cache
        env:
          CF_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN }}
        run: |
          cf cache purge --zone example.com --everything --yes
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.SS "Example B: Automated Workers Script Deployment"
Deploy a serverless Worker bundle and configure its route:
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
name: Deploy Worker

on:
  release:
    types: [published]

jobs:
  worker:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Setup Node
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: 20

      - name: Install cf CLI
        run: npm install -g @agileguy/cf-cli

      - name: Deploy Worker Bundle
        env:
          CF_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CF_WORKER_DEPLOY_TOKEN }}
          CF_ACCOUNT_ID: ${{ secrets.CF_ACCOUNT_ID }}
        run: |
          cf workers deploy --name production-api --file dist/worker.js --yes
          cf workers routes create --zone example.com --pattern "api.example.com/*" --script production-api
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.SS "Example C: D1 Database Migration Pipeline"
Execute schema migrations against a Cloudflare D1 SQL database:
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
name: Database Migration

on:
  push:
    paths:
      - "migrations/**"

jobs:
  migrate:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Install cf CLI
        run: npm install -g @agileguy/cf-cli

      - name: Run SQL Migration
        env:
          CF_API_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN }}
        run: |
          for file in migrations/*.sql; do
            echo "Executing $file..."
            cf d1 execute --database prod-db --file "$file"
          done
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
